`build/keypad.ino.hex` is built from `firmware/keypad/keypad.ino` for the ATmega328P at 16 MHz.
It links the standard AVR runtime, version 1.8.6. The runtime is free software under the GNU
Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or any later version, whose text is in
LICENSE-runtime. Its source is the archive at

https://orbefab.com/embedded/sources/avr-1.8.6.tar.bz2

with SHA-256 ff1d17274b5a952f172074bd36c3924336baefded0232e10982f8999c2f7c3b6, served with this
image. It is the archive Arduino publishes at
https://downloads.arduino.cc/cores/staging/avr-1.8.6.tar.bz2. The image was
built with avr-gcc 7.3.0-atmel3.6.1-arduino7 by packages/engine/scripts/sketches.sh in
https://github.com/orbefab/embedded, which pins both archives and relinks the sketch and the
runtime, so the image can be rebuilt against a modified runtime. The sketch is under MIT or
Apache-2.0, and those terms permit modifying the image and reverse engineering it to debug such
modifications.

The image also links the Arduino Keypad library 3.1.1 (Mark Stanley and Alexander Brevig,
maintained at Chris--A/Keypad), whose source files carry LGPL-2.1 headers and whose repository
carries the GNU General Public License, version 3 (GPL-3.0-only), whose text is in
LICENSE-keypad. Its source is the archive at
https://github.com/Chris--A/Keypad/archive/refs/tags/3.1.1.tar.gz
with SHA-256 07f89b5802e02d2b91554f0d2e7cf51016be1833315d066d1d87e179ecfa90d5. sketches.sh
pins that archive and relinks it with the sketch.

The image also holds the start-up code of the toolchain's C library, version 2.0.0, under that
library's modified BSD license, whose notice is in LICENSE-libc as the license requires, and
routines of GCC's runtime library (`libgcc`), under GPL-3.0-or-later with the GCC Runtime
Library Exception 3.1, whose text is in LICENSE-gcc-exception. That exception lets the compiled
runtime ship inside the program under the program's own terms.

These files and their licences:

`block.jsonc`, `README.md`, `scene.jsonc`, `firmware/NOTICE`, `firmware/keypad/keypad.ino` and
`tests/keypad.test` are under MIT OR Apache-2.0.

`build/keypad.ino.hex` links the runtime and Keypad, so it is under LGPL-2.1-or-later and GPL-3.0-only.
`firmware/LICENSE-runtime` is under LGPL-2.1-or-later.
`firmware/LICENSE-keypad` is under GPL-3.0-only.
`firmware/LICENSE-libc` is under BSD-3-Clause.
`firmware/LICENSE-gcc-exception` holds the GCC Runtime Library Exception 3.1
(GPL-3.0-or-later WITH GCC-exception-3.1).
